  "title": "NTLMSSP: Check for negative offsets",
  "description": "NTLMSSP has a unsigned 32 bit number that is used to mean an offset.\ntvbs have signed 32 bit offsets; negative numbers mean \"backwards from\nthe end of the tvb\" which isn't what this means. Throw an exception\nif the retrieved offset is signed, to avoid undefined behavior,\nadding the wrong bytes as a string, and possibly even moving backwards.\n\nOSS-Fuzz 451333962",
